<title>FINLAND: HARTWALL, PRIPPS TO BUY SHARE IN RUSSIAN BREWERY.</title>
<headline>HARTWALL, PRIPPS TO BUY SHARE IN RUSSIAN BREWERY.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baltic Beverages Holding Ab (BBH) owned by Finnish Hartwall and Swedish-Norwegian Pripps Ringes said on Friday it planned to acquire 50 percent of Russian brewery Taopin in an $11 million investment.</p>
<p>&quot;BBH will receive 50 percent of the brewery's shares in return for a $11 million investment programme,&quot; Hartwall said in a statement.</p>
<p>Annual production of the brewery is around 60 million litres, of which beers account for 90 percent, Hartwall said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240</p>
</text>
